{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-p3:000055:note_appended:sase-p3.2:031a0cbbe1d110135b245e38acc94139545d1f35c97dea5e8005bfa3911d3b41","timestamp":"2026-08-17T23:50:40Z","actor":"sase-p3.2","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"sase-p3.2","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Landed in sase-core as 82b10b5e43da7a1828e97554ae4a1416f3946e74 (feat(task_type): add spec validation, digest, and body rendering)."}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-p3:000056:note_appended:sase-p3.2:00e393a95c54a6394d2d0b715cb9b09892ba1264963827867b8782ff829cc67a","timestamp":"2026-08-17T23:50:56Z","actor":"sase-p3.2","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"sase-p3.2","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Added TaskTypeSpecWire and TaskTypeFieldSpecWire at schema_version 1, reusing the scalar subset of PROPERTY_TYPES. Verified reserved slugs, 120/400 caps, single-cell glyphs, #RRGGBB accents, unique snake_case fields, role subsets, per-type validator keys, compiling regex patterns, and template-placeholder membership. Digest is a stable sha256 over the normalized spec. Field-value validation returns one typed error per missing/unknown/invalid problem. Body rendering substitutes {{ name }} and is empty without a template. Snapshot parse/serialize is deterministic (types sorted by slug, no package version). Python bindings expose validate_task_type_spec, task_type_spec_digest, validate_task_type_field_values, render_task_type_body, parse_task_type_snapshot, and serialize_task_type_snapshot. sase-core just check (fmt, clippy, cargo test --workspace including sase_core_py) passed. Landed on sase-core master as 82b10b5e43da7a1828e97554ae4a1416f3946e74."}}
